# Path-level redirects for Cloudflare static assets.
#
# Only relative (path) rules are valid here — Cloudflare rejects absolute URLs
# in this file. Add any legacy-URL redirects for the client's old site below,
# one per line, e.g.:
#
#   /old-services-page/  /services/  301
#
# HOST CANONICALISATION (guide Part 7.4: www/non-www collapse to one form) is a
# zone-level setting, not a rule in this file. In the Cloudflare dashboard for
# the domain, set up:
#
#   1. Rules → Redirect Rules → a 301 from www.<domain>/* to <domain>/:splat
#      (or the reverse — whichever direction matches `site` in
#      astro.config.mjs, since that value generates every canonical tag)
#   2. SSL/TLS → Edge Certificates → "Always Use HTTPS" enabled
#
# Trailing slashes are already handled by Astro's `trailingSlash: 'always'`
# together with directory-format output.
